{"article_ids": ["868cd9841af624b4"], "canonical_title": "META-IR: Meta-Introspective Reasoning for Adaptive Safety Alignment in LLM", "category": "research", "confidence": 0.85, "description": "The paper presents META-IR, a meta‑introspective reasoning framework that enables large language models to adapt their safety alignment in real time. Unlike static alignment pipelines and fixed self‑evaluation policies such as STAIR, META‑IR can rapidly adjust to evolving manipulation strategies and adversarial distribution shifts, aiming to reduce jailbreak and harmful‑content vulnerabilities.", "entities": ["org:meta", "term:ir", "term:meta", "term:stair"], "first_seen": "2026-11-10T05:00:00Z", "id": "evt_868cd9841af624b4", "importance_score": 6.29, "last_updated": "2026-11-10T05:00:00Z", "source_ids": ["arxiv-cs-ai"]}
{"article_ids": ["7d1e00daeb767a07"], "canonical_title": "How CrossnoKaye grounds physical AI with Amazon Bedrock AgentCore", "category": "ai_agents", "confidence": 0.9, "description": "CrossnoKaye integrated Amazon Bedrock AgentCore into its ATLAS platform and AURA agentic system. The integration grounds AI reasoning in live plant data and runs Python code in isolated AgentCore sandboxes, producing checkable, math‑backed answers for plant engineers instead of unverified model guesses.", "entities": ["org:amazon", "term:atlas", "term:aura"], "first_seen": "2026-11-09T18:55:43Z", "id": "evt_7d1e00daeb767a07", "importance_score": 6.09, "last_updated": "2026-11-09T18:55:43Z", "source_ids": ["aws-machine-learning"]}
{"article_ids": ["9a8fde6cfa9ab68c"], "canonical_title": "llm-anthropic 0.31", "category": "model_release", "confidence": 0.95, "description": "Anthropic released two new language‑model versions, Fable 5.2 and Mythos 5.2. The llm‑anthropic 0.31 package was updated to include them, and the release notes note that Fable 5.2 currently ranks first on the Artificial Analysis leaderboard. Anthropic claims the models solve two open problems in black‑hole physics.", "entities": ["org:anthropic"], "first_seen": "2026-11-09T23:58:46Z", "id": "evt_9a8fde6cfa9ab68c", "importance_score": 6.087, "last_updated": "2026-11-09T23:58:46Z", "source_ids": ["simon-willison"]}
{"article_ids": ["2404a84292dfc861"], "canonical_title": "PACE: Keeping the Right Tokens in the KV Cache Is Not Enough for Long-Horizon LLM Agents", "category": "research", "confidence": 0.62, "description": "The paper \"PACE: Keeping the Right Tokens in the KV Cache Is Not Enough for Long-Horizon LLM Agents\" shows that existing eviction methods, which aim to retain tokens a later step will need, do not guarantee good performance when agents process sessions of up to millions of tokens. In experiments with 100,000‑token coding sessions on the Qwen3‑8B model using a 2,048‑token KV cache budget, a planner‑guided policy that keeps certain tokens still fails to meet the task demands, indicating that simply keeping the \"right\" tokens is not enough.", "entities": ["term:kv", "term:pace"], "first_seen": "2026-11-10T05:00:00Z", "id": "evt_2404a84292dfc861", "importance_score": 5.99, "last_updated": "2026-11-10T05:00:00Z", "source_ids": ["arxiv-cs-lg"]}
{"article_ids": ["0809cdc4ea32e509"], "canonical_title": "Ensemble Routing for Prompt-Adaptive Cost-Aware LLM Inference", "category": "research", "confidence": 0.85, "description": "The paper introduces PISA, a prompt‑adaptive, cost‑aware router that selects a single LLM for each request, and PISA‑E, an extension that dynamically composes ensembles of models. Unlike traditional routing that fixes one model per prompt or uses static ensembles, PISA evaluates each prompt’s characteristics and a cost budget to choose the most appropriate model or ensemble, aiming to balance response quality with inference cost.", "entities": ["term:pisa"], "first_seen": "2026-11-10T05:00:00Z", "id": "evt_0809cdc4ea32e509", "importance_score": 5.74, "last_updated": "2026-11-10T05:00:00Z", "source_ids": ["arxiv-cs-ai"]}
